IvPFunction* BHV_HoldSpeed::onRunState()
{
  ZAIC_PEAK zaic(m_domain, "speed");

  zaic.setSummit(m_speed);
  zaic.setPeakWidth(0.1);
  zaic.setBaseWidth(0.4);
  zaic.setSummitDelta(0.0);

  if(!zaic.stateOK()) {
    postWMessage(zaic.getWarnings());
    return nullptr;
  }

  IvPFunction* ipf = zaic.extractIvPFunction();

  if(ipf)
    ipf->setPWT(m_priority_wt);

  return ipf;
}
```

The key missing MOOS-IvP pieces are:

- construct the ZAIC with `m_domain`
- check `stateOK()` and post warnings
- set the behavior priority weight with `ipf->setPWT(m_priority_wt)`

The exact `PeakWidth`, `BaseWidth`, and `SummitDelta` values can be tuned or made behavior parameters, but the pattern above is the normal complete form.
